Every step section — first wave and later wave alike — hands its agent one fetch command,
`booping render-playbook {name} --step {step}`, never a link to read. The step bodies name a config
key and stay out of the composed render entirely: `jinja: true` renders the preamble, not the
bodies.

Twin of `fetch-lines-are-identical-without-jinja.txtar`, which plants the same playbook without
`jinja: true`; the two pinned stdouts are byte-identical.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  fx_label: hermetic label
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-fetch/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-fetch
title: Fetch
summary: Two waves of detached steps.
jinja: true
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-fetch/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  first: []
  second: [first]
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-fetch/first/prompt.md --
---
name: first
summary: First summary.
detached: sonnet:medium
---

Wave-one body, label {{ config.core.fx_label }}.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-fetch/second/prompt.md --
---
name: second
summary: Second summary.
detached: sonnet:medium
---

Wave-two body, label {{ config.core.fx_label }}.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-fetch
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
Preamble.

## Playbook Steps

Execute the steps in the most effective order considering their dependencies.

| Step | Dependencies | Summary | Review gate |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `first` | — | First summary. | — |
| `second` | `first` | Second summary. | — |

## Step: First

First summary.

Tell a sub-agent — model sonnet, effort medium — to get its instructions by calling this command: `booping render-playbook fx-fetch --step first`.

## Step: Second

Second summary.

